== Notes ==
* The{{i|Brimstone}}  fired by Vis will damage other non-Vis enemies.
* The Vis and its variations might be the most useful and powerful enemies when they are charmed, spawned by {{i|Friendly Ball}}, or {{i|Poke Go}}, since its {{i|Brimstone}} Laser is very powerful and can very quickly kill enemies and even bosses.

== Trivia ==
* In the original ''Binding Of Isaac'', if a Vis or a Double Vis was a [[Champion]], its {{i|Brimstone}} would be colored.
* {{E|Gluttony}} is a Vis with a head.
** Similarly, {{E|Super Gluttony}} is a Double Vis with a large head.
*** {{dlc|r}} Both's updated sprites use the new Vis/Double Vis sprites as well
** {{C|Tainted Lilith}}'s body is a black colored Vis with ribs added when opened.
* {{E|The Cage}} can spawn Vis with a unique coloration but no change to their behavior.
* Their designs are based on the {{E|Sisters Vis}}, which originated from ''[[wikipedia:Gish (video game)|Gish]]'', one of Edmund McMillen's other games.
* "Vis" may potentially serve as an abbreviation for the term "viscera", whereas "Evis" is likely an abbreviation for "eviscerated".
* If a Chubber is a champion, only the Vis part is colored and the Charger stays the same.
* {{dlc|r}}The name "Vis Versa" is a play on the term "vice versa", which is Latin for "the other way around".
* {{dlc|r}}The [[anti:Vis Versa|Vis Versa]] and [[anti:Evis|Evis]] both first appeared in the ''Antibirth'' mod.
** In  ''Antibirth'' the Vis Versa could spawn in {{S|Dark Room}}.

